# What must never reach an image.
#
# .env is first and is the reason this file exists. Keys are supplied by the
# platform at run time; one baked into a layer is in the registry forever, and
# `docker history` will show it to anyone who can pull the image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Uploaded policy schedules. Encrypted, but they are still other people's
# financial documents and they have no business in a build context.
apps/api/.vault/

node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
.git
.gitignore

# The deck, its mockups and the ETL's downloads. Hundreds of megabytes that no
# service reads at run time, and every one of them slows a build.
presentation deck/
etl/raw/
*.log
